course: dictionary
lesson: 10006
title: Telltale clues and telltale children
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Telltale has two meanings, and the context tells you which one. «The telltale crumbs on his face showed he had eaten the cake.» Here telltale is an adjective: the crumbs are a small clue that shows something has happened.
explain: Telltale can also be a noun, meaning a child who tells adults about other children's naughty behaviour. «Nobody wanted to sit next to the telltale» tells you the other children did not like it. In the US this is called a tattletale.
explain: Telling a grown-up when someone is hurt, in danger or being bullied is not being a telltale. It is the right thing to do. Ask yourself whether the telling is about a silly game or about keeping someone safe.
fact: Telltale (adjective) means a small clue that shows something is true or has happened.
fact: «Telltale signs» can show that an illness is starting or that rain is coming.
fact: Telltale (noun, UK and Australia) means a child who tells adults about other children's naughty behaviour. In the US it is a tattletale.
fact: «Telltale tit!» is a playground rhyme children use to tease someone who has told on others.
fact: «Yabeda» and «narc» both mean telltale or snitch, and kids often hate being called either.
exercise: Detective Maya finds «telltale crumbs» on the carpet. What does telltale mean here? | A kind of cake | A loud noise | *A small clue that shows something has happened | A new friend
exercise: «Dan told the teacher who broke the window, and the others called him a telltale.» What is a telltale in this sentence? | A famous detective | A window cleaner | *A child who tells adults about other children's naughty behaviour | A kind of fish
exercise: Ella sees Sam being bullied at lunch and tells a grown-up. Is this being a telltale? | Yes, always keep quiet | Only if Sam asks her to | Yes, but only if it is funny | *No, telling a grown-up about bullying is the right thing to do
test: «The doctor noticed the telltale spots and asked about the sore throat.» What do the telltale spots show? | A new game to play | A kind of cake | *A clue that shows an illness | A loud noise in the room
test: Which word in the examples means the same as telltale? | sleepy | brave | painted | *snitch
exam: «The telltale signs of rain were grey clouds and a cold wind.» What do the signs show? | That the cake is ready | *That rain is coming | That it is snowing in summer | That the sun will come out soon
